                <pb facs="0457" n="1043" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p2/pg1043"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On June 13, 1949, the United States and the Republic of Korea signed at Seoul an
                    agreement covering claims for electric power whereby the United States
                    transferred to the Republic goods, credits, and funds which had been set aside
                    by the United States Government <pb facs="0458" n="1044" xml:id="pg1044"/> for
                    the settlement of claims arising from the delivery to South Korea of electric
                    power from facilities in North Korea during the period from August 16, 1945, to
                    May 14, 1948. In return for the transfer of goods, credits, and funds, the
                    Republic of Korea agreed to assume responsibility for the settlement of any
                    claims arising from the delivery of the electric power.</p>
                <p>The treaty entered into force on December 28, 1949. The text is printed as TIAS
                    No. 4026 in <hi rendition="#italic">United States Treaties and Other
                        International Agreements</hi> (UST), volume 9, page 509.</p>
                <p>For background, see <ref target="frus:frus1948v06/pg_1214">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1948, volume VI, especially
                        telegram 417, June 2, from Seoul, page 1214</ref>; <ref
                        target="frus:frus1948v06/pg_1227">telegram 716, June 24, to Moscow, page
                        1227</ref>; and <ref target="frus:frus1948v06/pg_1252">telegram 1384, July
                        21, from Moscow, page 1252</ref>.</p>
            </div>
